I am a Storyteller in every aspect of my  life from my career to what I've done  wrestling what films being a film  producer being an actor and through my  tattoos I tell the story of my life  if people ask me how many tattoos I have  I typically say like three because most  of them are just all connected together  I consider like one big tattoo my back I  did in big chunks throughout my  wrestling career but I had to because I  was wrestling so much that I couldn't  take the time needed to to let them heal  I did my back and I let it set for so  long without finishing that I had to go  back and retrace and do my whole back  over again so my tattoo on my back I've  got to have close to 50 hours on my back  just because I had to go over it so many  times from letting it sit so long and  not getting it finished if you notice  throughout my career whenever I got  injured and I was out for two three  months I would always come back with new  tattoos which the company actually loved  because the more new tattoos you have  the more new action figures you have so  you can kind of date my wrestling career  through my tattoos and through my the  tattoos all my action figures I talk a  lot about Guardians of the Galaxy really  not just changing my career but changing  my life because it really just gave me a  second shot because when I left  wrestling I literally lost everything  and I left it to go into acting but I  struggled for about three years because  I just couldn't get work I couldn't even  get an agent but I finally I landed that  part and it just after that I just my  phone started ringing and I never I've  been a working actor ever since I did  the first Guardians of the Galaxy the  makeup process also changed a lot  throughout the years for the first film  which was the hardest film the makeup  process typically took about five discus  hours to put on the application and  about two hours to take it off so I  spent most of my day on set but uh  actually in the makeup chair so I was  there before everybody got there and I  was there well after everybody left and  didn't get much sleep and when I looked  back on it I don't know how I made it  through that film and I was so you know  happy and grateful to be there that I  wasn't really looking at it as a  hardship it was just a huge opportunity  for me my first tattoo I immediately  break out and sweat when anybody asked  me that it's long gone I'm it's not my  proudest moment but when I was 18 years  old and Tattoos weren't as common then I  went to the local tattoo shop which  wasn't a very nice place and they  typically weren't at that time there was  this old biker named Rick who uh  I gave you my first tattoo and it was  this heart that looked like it was  cement and around it it said Heart of  Stone  and I saw it and I thought yeah that's  tough so he said well where do you want  it and I said well  uh I want it on my ass because I don't  want my dad to see it I don't want to  get in trouble and he did it he put  harder Stone on my ass and I immediately  regretted it and I lived with it for  years and got Razz so much through my  wrestling career take a shower with the  20 other wrestlers who are just  Relentless I finally got it covered up  it was just I have a cherry blossom tree  on my back and I said well just extend  it down and make the roots a cover-up so  that's what I did I have the roots of a  cherry blossom tree that covered up my  heart stone I have a lot of cover-ups I  think cover-ups are again a part of your  story part of your life story you know  you have regrets you make mistakes and  so you try to fix them as best you can  and that's what they are in my cover-ups  are repairs of mistakes this is a  cover-up that was actually a  girlfriend's name this is an ex-wife's  name and my mom always said don't don't  put a woman's name on you and I didn't  listen and so here they are cover-ups  but yeah let me learn oh so this one it  used to be a team logo I was a part of a  team of person I considered a friend and  someone I really looked up to and then  he uh later came out publicly so with  some anti-gay statements and you know  turned out to be you know an extreme  homophobe and so I had a huge issue with  it it's a personalized with me my mom's  a lesbian and I just can no longer call  him a friend and so I had it covered up  with with this oh my most painful so  that's a toss-up that's between uh my  feet which hurt they were torturous in  the back of my knee here the back of  this knee I actually started drinking in  the middle of this tattoo because my  tattoo artist was actually doing it at  my house and I said just give me a few  minutes I went and and took a shot came  back and it still kept hurting so I went  and took a couple more shots came back  he got back into it and I finally said  dude you gotta leave get out of my house  so I actually never finished this tattoo  the other one saw or my feet they just  weren't as big but they were just as  painful but I was able to get through  these in the city but they they hurt  they were torture so the tattoo that  took the longest to heal was actually  this one on my elbow and the reason it  took so long to heal is because my  tattoo artist put it on and I looked at  it in the mirror and I said that doesn't  look right so we put this stencil up  next to it and realize that he put it on  backwards he wasn't so nonchalant about  him saying not a big deal we'll fix it  so what he did was he Whited it out and  then he tattooed it on again so it's  like getting three tattoos in one day in  an area that's pretty sensitive so it's  swelled out like a balloon and it took  weeks for the swelling to go down but  that is by far it took the longest to  heal this tattoo here which is a Gracie  fighter symbol you know I have some are  very personal to me and you know some  are just things I liked when I was  growing up things I was a fan of I have  some you know Avengers and Guardians  which are personal to me but I expect  her was also very personal media film I  did James Bond film and I have a Wu-Tang  Clan Rizza from a routine Clan the  originator of the Wu-Tang Clan actually  helped me get my start in films Batman  just because I love him Rockstar because  yeah my favorite tattoo is uh this one  there's a portrait of my dogs my older  dogs I have three new dogs um we lost  him both to cancer she's still with my  ex-wife but she's older now but I am  going to get a save room for my newer  dogs I was always you really just taught  to be proud of my Heritage my mom's  Greek my dad's Filipino I didn't really  have close ties to my family but I just  saw even my mom was just always made me  very aware of who I was what my  background was to always be proud of  that and so I always kind of embrace  that being half Greek and half Filipino  always very proud of my roots and I  display it on my body a Filipino thing  Greek flag and I'll show another  Filipino flag and another Filipino son I  think I really embraced it when I was  older and when I got to visit the  Philippines and when I got to visit  Greece and just kind of kind of a  homecoming feeling especially when I  went to the Philippines for the first  time but I'm only half Filipino from the  United States but they embraced me like  I was 100 Filipino and I was born and  raised there you know that experience is  never going to make me feel anything  less in my life it's just it's just a  dream like it's just so surreal to go  there to a country and have them just  treat you like you know it's You're The  Prodigal Son  I have a few that didn't a few tattoos  that didn't turn out quite the way I  wanted so I have you know this one this  raven is not exactly one I wanted this  raven to look a lot more menacing but I  also have this tattoo here and I found  this really cool picture that I loved  and I really always always wanted to do  this gentlemen hooligan because I kind  of always felt like who I was I'm really  from the streets I grew up poor and that  was kind of life I knew until I was in  my 30s but I always consider myself a  gentleman as well I give a lot of  respect to people just because that's  just the person I am that's how I was  raised but I found this cool picture and  it was Killian Murphy from peaky  blinders and I asked John to alter it so  it didn't look so much like Killian  Murphy and I got it and I thought okay  that doesn't look exactly like I have a  tattoo of killing a Murphy on my thigh  but the first time I posted it on my  social media all I got was oh my God  you've got a tattoo of Kelly Murphy well  yeah I guess I do  it is what it is I'm a fan so you know  you know a little embarrassed but not  ashamed so Killian there you go your  face is tattooed on my thigh  I've Winnie the Pooh tattoo on the back  of my leg which I get asked about a lot  so I did a film uh called my spy with a  little actress named Chloe Coleman who  is one of my favorite people in the  world and so we went out on the Press  tour and at one uh Outlet we had to play  true or false to see how well we knew  each other they asked Chloe you said  true or false um Dave has a tattoo of  Winnie the Pooh and Chloe said well I  know you know most people might think  that Dave is is big and mean and scary  so he wouldn't have a Winnie the Pooh  tattoo but I know Dave he's like the  sweetest guy ever and he's just a big  teddy bear and I just love him to dance  she went on and on said all these great  things about me and she said so yes I  think it's true Dave has a Winnie the  Pooh tattoo and she was like got the  buzzer wrong and she was like oh she was  so disappointed and I was disappointed  for her and I said I don't have one but  because I love you so much I'm going to  get one so I got a one he is the Poo  tattoo for my little co-star Chloe  Coleman my latest tattoos were my two  neck tattoos so one is a Blade Runner  reference and the other is a Basquiat  Crown huge massive Phantom Bosque I was  by far my favorite artist they do have a  tattoo shop because it's always been a  dream of mine to own a tattoo shop just  because I love the culture I love the  environment I love sitting around tattoo  shops I love sitting around barber shops  I love the conversation that goes on the  camaraderie so the name of my tattoo  shop is DC Society Inc DC has a double  moniker for me it's uh I'm from  Washington DC but also stands for Dream  Chaser which I have used that hashtag  for years on my uh social media that's  kind of the way I look at my life I've  just chased my dreams no matter what  they were how crazy they seemed and uh  you know for some reason it seems to  work out for me
 

